# ============================================================
# .cursorrules — okengine
# One law. Eight elements. One contract.
# The backend model stays small; operational surfaces are derived from it.
# ============================================================

# ---------- Runtime & Tooling ----------
- okengine requires Bun &gt;=1.4.2. All code MUST be ESNext ESM modules (no CommonJS).
- Use `bun test` for tests, `oxlint` for linting, `oxfmt` for formatting.
- TypeScript strict mode is enforced: `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noImplicitOverride`, `erasableSyntaxOnly`.
- Prefer `verbatimModuleSyntax: true` — use `import type` for type-only imports.
- `allowImportingTsExtensions` is enabled; import `.ts` files directly without `.js` rewrite.

# ---------- Core Philosophy ----------
- Every backend behavior is a Flow: `on(Trigger) -&gt; Effects` via the `fx` surface.
- The 8 elements are the ONLY vocabulary: flow, signal, store, clock, gate, vault, channel, ai.
- Effects must be EXPLICITLY declared: reads, writes, emits, sends, asks, secrets, calls.
- The Manifest is DERIVED from source — never hand-edit `manifest.v1.schema.json`.
- Client, Console, and MCP are derived from the same Manifest — no separate codegen.

# ---------- Imports & Public API ----------
- The core programming vocabulary is 10 named values from `okengine`:
  `on`, `flow`, `signal`, `store`, `clock`, `gate`, `vault`, `channel`, `ai`, `plugin`
- World access goes through `fx` — effects are inferred.
- Use `zod` for all runtime schema validation.
- Use `drizzle-orm` for database operations; prefer `store.resource` for declarative CRUD.
- Use `drizzle-orm/zod` to bridge Drizzle tables with Zod when needed.

# ---------- Flow Patterns ----------
- A Flow with no trigger is call-only (internal / private).
- Triggers: `http`, `signal`, `cron`, `every`, `cdc`.
- Effects `reads` / `writes` use ResourceRef format: `sql:table`, `kv:namespace`, `files:bucket`, `index:name`.
- Effects `emits` reference Signal names; `sends` reference Template names; `asks` reference Prompt names.
- Effects `secrets` reference SecretContract names (capabilities, never values).
- Effects `calls` reference other Flow names for transitive composition.
- Declare `plane: "user"` or `plane: "operator"` when applicable.
- Use `durable: true` + named `steps` for long-running / retryable flows.

# ---------- Store Patterns ----------
- Store facets: `sql`, `kv`, `files`, `index`.
- Prefer `store.resource` over hand-written Drizzle schemas for standard CRUD.
- If hand-writing schema, place it in a `schema.ts` and use Drizzle's column builders.
- Use `field.*` helpers (e.g., `field.text()`, `field.integer()`) when available.
- Classify columns with `pii`, `sensitive`, and `retain` tags where applicable.

# ---------- Gate Patterns ----------
- Gate kinds: `policy` (auth/roles) or `rate` (throttling).
- Rate strategies: `sliding-window-counter`, `fixed-window`, `sliding-log`, `token-bucket`, `leaky-bucket`.
- Use `gate.public` for unauthenticated endpoints.
- Reference gates in Flows via the `gates` array.

# ---------- Signal Patterns ----------
- Signal delivery helpers are MANDATORY: `signal.once`, `signal.broadcast`, `signal.live` (like `http.get` / `http.post`).
- Declare `retries`, `deadLetter`, and `schema` explicitly when needed.

# ---------- AI Patterns ----------
- AI config lives under the `ai` element in the manifest.
- Define `models`, `prompts`, and `agents` separately.
- Prompts support `budget` (maxCostPerCall, maxCostPerRun), `evals`, and version pinning.
- Agents declare `tools` (FlowRef array), `maxSteps`, and `model`.

# ---------- Console UI (React + Vite + Tailwind) ----------
- Console UI source lives in `src/console/ui-next/` — separate from backend logic.
- Console is a Vite SPA built with React, TailwindCSS v4, and TanStack Router.
- Do NOT mix backend Flow logic with Console UI components.
- Console runs on port `:6533`; Vite HMR on `:6537` (`bun run dev:console`).

# ---------- Drivers ----------
- Drivers are protocol-named and keyed by environment in the manifest.
- When adding a driver, register it properly in `src/drivers/` and update exports.
- Supported drivers include SQL (pglite, libsql), KV, files, index, vault, channel, AI providers.

# ---------- Database & Migrations ----------
- Use `oke db push` for local dev schema sync (auto-pushes in `oke dev`).
- Use `oke db generate` or `oke db migrate` for production migrations.
- Drizzle Kit is the migration tool; config is in `drizzle.config.ts`.

# ---------- Testing & CI ----------
- Use `bun test --pass-with-no-tests` as the default test runner for targeted tests.
- Playwright is used for Console smoke tests (`tests/console/smoke.spec.ts`).
- Budget tests exist for kernel, client, console, and runtime — respect them.
- Fixtures for compiler tests live in `src/compiler/fixtures/` — excluded from tsconfig.
- NEVER run `bun run ci` automatically after finishing an implementation. Only run `bun run ci` when the user explicitly asks for CI / pre-push gate.

# ---------- Post-Implementation & Changelog ----------
- After completing ANY implementation (feature, bug fix, refactor, CLI, driver, plugins, etc.), ALWAYS update `changelog.md` under `## Unreleased`.
- Place bullets under the appropriate group (`### ✨ Added`, `### 💥 Breaking Changes`, `### ♻️ Changed`, `### ⚠️ Deprecated`, `### 🔥 Removed`, `### 🐛 Fixed`, `### 🔒 Security`) and `####` area (e.g., `Console — Chrome`, `Console — Observability`, `Console — Store`, `Console — Vault`, `Console — Flows & traces`, `Console — Units & Call API`, `Console — Auth & shell`, `Runtime`, `Dev, Keel & create-oke`, `Docs`).
- Never append to an already-released `## vX.Y.Z` section.
- Version bump is separate (`bun run bump`).

# ---------- Monorepo Structure ----------
- Workspaces: `packages/*` and `site`.
- `packages/create-oke` is the scaffolding CLI.
- `site` is the Next.js docs site — do NOT mix with framework source.
- Keep changes scoped to the relevant workspace.

# ---------- Code Style ----------
- Prefer explicit types over inference for public API surfaces.
- Use `const` assertions for literal unions where applicable.
- Keep Flow definitions declarative and close to the `on()` call.
- Avoid `any` — the project enforces strict TypeScript.
- Use `oxlint` rules; do not introduce lint errors.

# ---------- What NOT to do ----------
- Do NOT run `bun run ci` automatically after finishing tasks unless the user explicitly requested it.
- Do NOT import from `node_modules` paths directly — always use package names.
- Do NOT hand-edit `manifest.v1.schema.json` — it is a derived artifact.
- Do NOT use CommonJS (`require`, `module.exports`) anywhere.
- Do NOT add implicit effects — every read, write, emit, send, ask, secret, or call must be declared.
- Do NOT pollute the `okengine` public exports with internal utilities.
- Do NOT modify `src/console/ui-next/dist/` — it is a build output.